## Iterating on an existing prototype

Load only what the change requires:

- Visual / component change → `docs/LOFI_KIT_PATTERNS.md` + `docs/COMPOSITION_PATTERNS.md`
- Flow / behaviour change → `docs/UX_PATTERNS.md`
- Brief translation → `docs/NL_COMPONENT_MAPPING_LO_FI.md` first, then both

Do not reload `docs/INSTRUCTIONS.md` unless the scope of the change is large
enough to require re-reading the full brief.

- When editing an existing file, check whether it imports from `lofi-kit`.
  If it does not, migrate the elements you touch to lofi-kit components.
  Do not leave a file half-migrated — if you open it, bring the touched areas
  into compliance.

---

## Flow rules (summary — full rules in `docs/UX_PATTERNS.md`)

These are the most commonly violated rules. They are enforced here as a
reminder, not a replacement for reading the full file.

- **Confirmation on every meaningful action.** Save, Create, Remove, Add to
  roster, Mark as Redundant, Discard Changes. If unsure, add a confirmation.
- **Save/Create buttons start disabled.** Enable only when all required
  validations pass and at least one change has been made.
- **Validation is inline.** Each field/row shows its own adjacent error message.
  No summary banners. Validate on blur; re-validate on change if already in
  error.
- **Mocked data is real-world.** Real team names, real competitions, real player
  archetypes. Never `Team 1`, `Player A`, `Test Record`.
- **Timestamps:** `DD MMM YYYY, HH:mm` (e.g. `07 Apr 2026, 14:32`).
- **User handles:** `j.smith` format.
- **Every data-modifying action appends a changelog entry** in real time.

